    "result_text": "All 263 tests pass. The change is complete and green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `salutation` feature: `POST /api/owners` accepts an optional `title` (MR/MRS/MS/DR), which is persisted and read back as `salutation` = `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\nChanges:\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `title` (input/stored) to the `OwnerFields` schema and read-only `salutation` to the `Owner` schema. These generate the `title` and `salutation` fields on `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto`.\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `title` column with getter/setter so the value persists.\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a read-time `salutation(owner)` derivation and wired it via `@Mapping`. `title` maps automatically by name in both directions.\n- **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `title` column to the `owners` table.\n\nThe write path flows through the existing OfficeFloor pipeline unchanged: `BuildOwner` maps the request DTO (including `title`) into the `Owner`, `SaveOwner` persists it, and the GET pipeline's `RespondWithOwner` returns the DTO with the derived `salutation`. The acceptance test (`coreComposesSalutation`) and the full suite (263 tests) pass.",
